# Copy this file to dictionary.local to add RADIUS attributes that are not in
# the dictionaries shipped with PacketFence. It uses the FreeRADIUS dictionary
# format. FreeRADIUS reads it through raddb/dictionary and PacketFence uses the
# same definitions to send the attributes in RADIUS CoA and Disconnect requests
# (for example from the bounce, coa or disconnect scope of a switch template).
#
# Restart the RADIUS services, pfconfig, pfqueue, httpd.aaa and pfperl-api
# after a change.
#
# Example: Extreme-Dynamic-Config, the vendor-specific attribute of Extreme
# Networks Fabric Engine (vendor 1916, attribute 252). Sent in the coa or
# bounce scope of a switch template as "Extreme-Dynamic-Config = PORTBOUNCE",
# it bounces the port so the endpoint renews its DHCP address.
#
#BEGIN-VENDOR    Extreme
#ATTRIBUTE       Extreme-Dynamic-Config          252     string
#END-VENDOR      Extreme
